    [
      "text",
      "A payload that is not JSON still reaches the hook, which decides what it needs.",
      "clean"
    ],
    [
      "text",
      "Env is the repository and binary state a run needs.",
      "clean"
    ],
    [
      "text",
      "ExitUnknown is the exit code for a hook this binary does not know; a gate that cannot check\nmust not read as a pass.",
      "clean"
    ],
    [
      "text",
      "Func is one hook. stand is the optional second argument (for example pre or post).",
      "clean"
    ],
    [
      "text",
      "Package hook is the runtime behind `lighthouse hook <name> [stand]`: a registry of hooks, the\nexit codes and output they produce, and the notices that tell a session that the installed\nbinary and the repository disagree (spec, hook runtime).",
      "clean"
    ],
    [
      "text",
      "Payload is what the harness writes to stdin.",
      "clean"
    ],
    [
      "text",
      "Register adds a hook. It panics on a duplicate name: that is a programming error.",
      "clean"
    ],
    [
      "text",
      "Result is the outcome of a hook. Output is printed as JSON on stdout when it is not empty.",
      "clean"
    ],
    [
      "text",
      "Run runs hook name and returns the exit code. A result with code 0 gets the version and\nbuild notices added, once per session; a blocking result gets none, so the notice is not\nspent on a message the user reads next to a block.",
      "clean"
    ],
    [
      "text",
      "StateDir holds the once-per-session markers; empty means none is known, and the\nnotices stay quiet.",
      "clean"
    ],
    [
      "text",
      "buildHasFailed reports whether the build from lighthouse's own checkout at root failed.",
      "clean"
    ],
    [
      "text",
      "firstInSession reports whether kind was not yet shown in session, and records that it now is.\nThe claim is one exclusive create, so parallel calls of one session show it once. When the\nmarker cannot be written the notice is shown anyway: a repeated notice is better than a\nsilent one. Without a state directory there is no private place for a marker at all, and\na notice on every hook call would drown the session: then it stays quiet.",
      "clean"
    ],
    [
      "text",
      "hasSource reports whether root is lighthouse's own checkout, the one place a binary is built.",
      "clean"
    ],
    [
      "text",
      "invoke runs f and turns a panic into a COULD NOT CHECK on errOut: a gate that crashed did not\ncheck, and exit 3 lets run.sh apply the blocking list.",
      "clean"
    ],
    [
      "text",
      "sourceMain marks lighthouse's own checkout: only there does a `dev` repo build its binary.",
      "clean"
    ],
    [
      "text",
      "tag is v with a v prefix; \"dev\", the version of a binary built from source, is no tag.",
      "clean"
    ],
    [
      "text",
      "withNotices joins the notices that are due after the systemMessage of the hook. The result is\noutput itself when nothing is due.",
